    "body": "Staff Ready Ops. Checklist Closing Operations Closing Closing Checklists Area Operations Owner Shift Lead Due Before leaving Date Shift Signed by Use the right close for the right team. BOH closes food, equipment, dish, safety, and storage. FOH closes the room, guest systems, service stations, money, and handover notes. Role notes below remove ambiguity. Open Google Form Your Role Checklist Reference BOH Closer BOH Line Cook BOH Prep Cook BOH Dishwasher FOH Host FOH Server FOH Bartender BOH Opener Department Closing Reference BOH Kitchen Closing FOH Room Closing FOH Payment & Cash-Up Switch Opening Checklists BOH Role Closing Check Line Cook Label, date, cover, and store station mise; discard expired or unsafe food Line Cook Clean grill, fryer exterior, hot line, cutting boards, pans, utensils, and station surfaces Line Cook Turn off assigned equipment and hand over low stock, prep needs, or repairs Prep Cook Wrap and label all prep, update prep list, and rotate product into correct storage Prep Cook Clean prep tables, scales, slicer or processor parts, sinks, labels, and storage bins Prep Cook Write tomorrow's prep priorities and flag shortages before leaving Dishwasher Run final dish loads, delime or drain as required, clean filters, screens, racks, and sinks Dishwasher Air-dry and store clean items; return smallwares to line, prep, bar, and service stations Dishwasher Sweep, mop, empty bins, reline cans, and leave dish area dry and reset Opener Ending a Shift Leave opening notes for tomorrow: equipment flags, prep gaps, product quality, and deliveries Opener Ending a Shift Confirm morning-only tasks were completed or handed over to the closer Opener Ending a Shift Restock opening supplies if the team will need them first thing tomorrow Closer Own BOH closing checklist submission and confirm all kitchen role closes are complete Closer Log final fridge, freezer, waste, equipment, cleaning, and security checks Closer Write manager handover before locking up or leaving the kitchen FOH Role Closing Check Server Close all tables, check payments, file receipts, report comps, and finish assigned sidework Server Reset section, polish cutlery/glassware, restock stations, and record guest issues Server Hand over VIPs, complaints, allergies, lost property, and maintenance notes Host Reconcile reservations, no-shows, waitlist notes, future bookings, and special requests Host Reset host stand, menus, table plan, coat area, entry, and waiting area Host Record guest feedback, accessibility needs, and table pacing issues for manager review Bartender Close tabs, reconcile bar payments, clean wells, discard or label garnish, and secure stock Bartender Restock glassware, napkins, straws, wine tools, mixers, and opening par where possible Bartender Write low stock, breakage, keg, wine, batch, and maintenance notes"
