    "body": "Staff Ready Ops. Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) DOH-ADV-09 DOH-Informed · Menu Advisory DOH Consumer Advisory Department / Area DOH-Informed Menu Advisory Prepared By Manager / PIC Date Reviewed June 2026 Version 1.0 NYC DOH source requirements for written consumer advisories when raw or undercooked animal foods are served or offered cooked to order. Key Actions Use the required written advisory for raw or undercooked meats, poultry, seafood, shellfish, or eggs. Mark or describe every menu item that is raw, undercooked, or cooked to order. Do not serve raw or undercooked animal foods to higher-risk facilities or populations covered by Article 81 limits. Review specials, brunch items, bar drinks, sauces, and seasonal menus before service. 1 Purpose Make sure guests receive the required written warning when menu items contain or may be served as raw or undercooked animal foods. 2 Scope Applies to DOH-Informed Menu Advisory and any staff member assigned to this process, task, equipment, checklist, or manager follow-up. 3 Responsibilities All assigned staff must follow this SOP exactly as written during the applicable task or shift. The responsible manager or team (Manager / PIC) is responsible for training staff, answering questions, and verifying that the procedure is followed. The shift lead or manager must stop the task and start corrective action when the standard cannot be met. 4 Definitions / Key Terms Term Definition SOP Standard Operating Procedure; the approved method for completing this task. Person in Charge The manager or certified lead responsible for supervising the task and making food safety decisions during the shift. Corrective Action The required response when a step, limit, record, or safety standard is missed or cannot be verified. 5 Materials / Equipment Needed The written advisory text must state: “Consuming raw or undercooked meats, poultry, seafood, shellfish or eggs may increase your risk of foodborne illness.” The advisory must appear on menus, menu boards, brochures, signage, table tents, placards, or other customer-facing menu materials where the food is offered. Any food that needs the advisory must be marked with an asterisk or other mark, or described as raw, undercooked, or cooked to order. The advisory applies to raw or undercooked meat, fish, molluscan shellfish, poultry, unpasteurized raw eggs, and foods containing those ingredients, including sauces, dressings, drinks, desserts, ceviche, sushi/sashimi, oysters, steak tartare, rare duck, and burgers or eggs cooked to order. Raw or undercooked meat, eggs, fish, or molluscan shellfish must not be served in facilities that primarily serve higher-risk persons, including immunocompromised persons, senior centers, charitable feeding programs, custodial care facilities, hospitals, adult day care, assisted living, child care, camps, preschools, and elementary/secondary schools. 6 Procedure (Step-by-Step) When To Check Before printing or publishing any menu. Before run"
