    "body": "Staff Ready Ops. Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) DOH-PEST-07 DOH-Informed · Facility Protection DOH Pest & Waste Control Department / Area DOH-Informed Facility Protection Prepared By Manager / PIC Date Reviewed June 2026 Version 1.0 Integrated pest management, daily pest evidence checks, waste handling, licensed pest control, and pesticide safety. Key Actions Inspect daily for pest evidence and conditions that attract pests. Remove food, water, harborage, and entry points. Keep refuse covered, clean, and away from food areas. Use licensed pest professionals and keep contract/service records available. 1 Purpose Prevent rodents, insects, and other pests from contaminating food, equipment, utensils, storage areas, and customer spaces. 2 Scope Applies to DOH-Informed Facility Protection and any staff member assigned to this process, task, equipment, checklist, or manager follow-up. 3 Responsibilities All assigned staff must follow this SOP exactly as written during the applicable task or shift. The responsible manager or team (Manager / PIC) is responsible for training staff, answering questions, and verifying that the procedure is followed. The shift lead or manager must stop the task and start corrective action when the standard cannot be met. 4 Definitions / Key Terms Term Definition SOP Standard Operating Procedure; the approved method for completing this task. Person in Charge The manager or certified lead responsible for supervising the task and making food safety decisions during the shift. Corrective Action The required response when a step, limit, record, or safety standard is missed or cannot be verified. 5 Materials / Equipment Needed Food service establishments must be kept free of pests and conditions conducive to pests. Managers must inspect the facility daily for pest presence and conditions that allow entry or harborage. A pest management professional contract and service records must be maintained and available. Preventive pest service must occur at least monthly where required by Article 81. Openings that allow pest entry must be sealed; door gaps may require sweeps or barriers, including tight thresholds. Pesticides may be applied only by properly licensed pest professionals. No spraying in food prep/service areas while food is exposed. Food-contact surfaces affected by pesticide application must be protected and cleaned/sanitized before reuse. 6 Procedure (Step-by-Step) When To Check During opening walk-through before food prep begins. During closing after cleaning and trash removal. After receiving deliveries and breaking down cardboard. Any time droppings, gnaw marks, insects, eggs, odors, grease buildup, standing water, or damaged doors/screens are observed. After pest control service to verify recommendations were handled. Step 1 - Inspect the outside first Check garbage area, delivery door, back door, drains, standing water, weeds, grease, and gaps that could attract or admit pests. Step 2 - Inspect food and storage area"
