    "body": "Staff Ready Ops. Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) DOH-RECV-06 DOH-Informed · Source & Storage DOH Receiving & Storage Department / Area DOH-Informed Source & Storage Prepared By Manager / PIC Date Reviewed June 2026 Version 1.0 Approved source, receiving temperatures, rejection rules, shellfish tags, storage order, labeling, FIFO, and dry storage controls. Key Actions Receive food only from approved sources. Reject unsafe, damaged, unlabeled, pest-contaminated, or temperature-abused deliveries. Keep shellfish tags for 90 days. Store food covered, labeled, off the floor, and protected from cross-contamination. 1 Purpose Stop unsafe food from entering the restaurant and protect accepted food during storage, rotation, and prep staging. 2 Scope Applies to DOH-Informed Source & Storage and any staff member assigned to this process, task, equipment, checklist, or manager follow-up. 3 Responsibilities All assigned staff must follow this SOP exactly as written during the applicable task or shift. The responsible manager or team (Manager / PIC) is responsible for training staff, answering questions, and verifying that the procedure is followed. The shift lead or manager must stop the task and start corrective action when the standard cannot be met. 4 Definitions / Key Terms Term Definition SOP Standard Operating Procedure; the approved method for completing this task. Person in Charge The manager or certified lead responsible for supervising the task and making food safety decisions during the shift. Corrective Action The required response when a step, limit, record, or safety standard is missed or cannot be verified. Food that requires time/temperature control for safety Food that must be controlled by time or temperature to limit pathogen growth or toxin production. HACCP Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Point; a written food safety plan required for certain specialized processes. 5 Materials / Equipment Needed Cold food that requires time/temperature control for safety at receiving: 41°F or below unless a specific food has a different standard. Smoked fish and applicable ROP foods: 38°F or below. Raw shell eggs: ambient delivery/storage target of 45°F or below. Frozen food: frozen solid, no large ice crystals, thawing, or refrozen appearance. Hot delivered food: 140°F or above. Shellfish must come from approved sources with shellfish tags; tags must be retained for 90 days. Meat and poultry must show inspection/approved source documentation where applicable. Dry storage should be clean, dry, ventilated, pest-free, and generally maintained around 70°F with about 50% humidity when possible. Food must be stored at least 6 inches off the floor and protected from splash, dust, chemicals, and pests. Do not perform reduced oxygen packaging, cook-chill, or sous vide unless the restaurant has prior Department approval and an approved HACCP plan for that food/process. 6 Procedure (Step-by-Step) When To Check At every delivery before the invoice is accepted"
