    "excerpt": "The closer is the last person responsible for the kitchen. When the close is done correctly, the opener walks in the next morning and everything is exactly where it needs to be. When it is not — a grill left dirty, knives not stored, a fridge door not shut — that problem lands on everyone the next d…",
